---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"blkdiscard\")"
---
Discard sectors on a block device.

Sends BLKDISCARD, BLKSECDISCARD, or BLKZEROOUT ioctls to tell the storage device that a range of
blocks is no longer in use.

Usage: blkdiscard [OPTIONS] <DEVICE>

Arguments:
  <DEVICE>
          Block device to operate on

Options:
  -f, --force
          Disable exclusive open mode (O_EXCL)

  -o, --offset <OFFSET>
          Byte offset to start discarding (default: 0)
          
          [default: 0]

  -l, --length <LENGTH>
          Number of bytes to discard (default: to end of device)

  -p, --step <STEP>
          Bytes to discard per ioctl call (default: all at once)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress warnings

  -s, --secure
          Secure discard (BLKSECDISCARD)

  -z, --zeroout
          Zero-fill instead of discard (BLKZEROOUT)

  -v, --verbose
          Show progress

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
